---
title: Volunteer at PyCascades
---
body:

Volunteer at PyCascades
----------------------------

PyCascades is a volunteer run conference. Without folks like you we would not be able to put on the event. We will be
looking to fill a number of roles, please read the brief descriptions below and if you are interested fill out the
volunteer sign up sheet `here <https://bit.ly/pycascades-volunteers-2021>`__.

**Chat Moderator**: Responsible for monitoring text and/or video chat rooms to
make sure everyone has a safe conference. We are also encouraging moderators to
encourage people to engage in conversation. (Time commitment: 1-4 hours flexible)

**Q/A Moderator**: Responsible for monitoring live chat in on the main stage to
gather questions asked by attendees watching to pass onto the Session Chair. (Time commitment: 2 hours)

**Session Chair**: Responsible for introducing speakers and breaks as well as
asking speakers questions gathered by the Q/A Moderator live. (Time commitment: 2 hours, video and public speaking required)

**Green Room**: On-call role for helping speakers and attendees troubleshoot video and audio issues. (Time commitment: 2-4 hours on-call)

If you are interested in volunteering for PyCascades please fill out the form
`here <https://bit.ly/pycascades-volunteers-2021>`__.
